Corpus

The corpus is the closed list of ROS message families Weld must handle, plus the order to generate them.

Families

builtin_interfaces, std_msgs, geometry_msgs, sensor_msgs plus SetCameraInfo, trajectory_msgs, nav_msgs with map services, stereo_msgs, shape_msgs, visualization_msgs, diagnostic_msgs, std_srvs. Point cloud Python helpers are utility code, not a codegen target.

Each entry carries:

- Package, Name, Kind (message or service; actions are out of scope for Phase 1)
- Summary (human only, never parsed)
- HeaderNote (header semantics only, empty when no header rule)
- Dependencies (direct package/name requirements, Header first, field order)
- HasHeader (direct std_msgs/Header field; Header itself is false)
- TypeHash (reserved RIHS01_..., empty in Phase 1)

Code: internal/types/corpus.go.

Order

Topological generation order:

builtin_interfaces then std_msgs then geometry_msgs then sensor_msgs plus trajectory_msgs plus nav_msgs then stereo plus shape plus visualization plus diagnostic.

Tests pin rank order plus a dependency DAG: every dependency index precedes its user, HasHeader implies a Header dependency and a non-empty header note, and header dependencies without HasHeader are rejected unless allow-listed.

Notes

Header notes are header only. Sentinel, enum, and lifetime hints live in Summary only. Examples:

- LaserScan notes first-ray stamp plus angles about positive Z from positive X
- Image notes optical frame acquisition
- Path notes path frame with per-pose headers as fallback
- NavSatFix notes ROS time in antenna frame
- Marker lifetime zero means forever is a per-element rule in Summary

Float sentinels are asserted from Summary: NaN means unmeasured on float fields only, discard outside range per message, IMU -1 disregard with all-zero unknown, zeroed camera matrices mean uncalibrated, occupancy bytes decode via resolution plus origin.

Sync

The manifest is manually synced to ROS IDL. The test file documents the source tree and distro link. To extend: add the entry with deps in field order, keep topo rank, add header and sentinel rows to the table tests, and keep the bounded-sequence uniqueness invariant (only SolidPrimitive is bounded).
